WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/system/components/CommandSearch.tsx — a CONTROLLED search box:
    <Input value onChange placeholder={t('commands.search.placeholder','Search commands...')}
           icon={<Search/>} /> .
  It owns no data hook of its own (prompt "Data sources: useTranslation"). Its behaviour is defined by its
  only caller, web/src/features/system/components/VehicleCommandCenter.tsx, which client-side filters the
  static COMMANDS catalog on every keystroke (synchronous useMemo, no debounce, no request):
      if (!search.trim()) return null;                  // empty box → favorites/categories (idle)
      const q = search.toLowerCase();
      COMMANDS.filter(c => t(label).toLowerCase().includes(q) || c.category.includes(q) || c.command.includes(q))
      → length>0 → tile grid (content) ; length===0 → t('commands.search.noResults','No commands match your search')
  The same surface carries the freshness/availability envelope the prompt's states map to:
    isLoading (command-status query)        → loading
    isStale  → t('commands.staleData','Vehicle data is {{age}} old. The vehicle may be asleep or offline.')
    isAsleep → "Wake it up first to send commands."   → offline

